<edge source="2D_SPECTROGRAM_c5807f7d" target="2D_SPECTROGRAM_c5807f7d" id="memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 50 (for th...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 50 (for th...)</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Consolidated summary at step 50 (for the last block of research):\n### **Strategic Lesson: The Efficiency-Accuracy Tradeoff**\n\n**Core Insight:** You've discovered that brute-force complexity (more layers/filters/parameters) improves accuracy but at rapidly diminishing returns and significant computational cost. The real signal lies in training stability - your best models achieved superior performance through lower learning rates and higher weight decay, not just larger architectures.\n\n**What to Keep:**\n- Maintain lower learning rates (~7e-5) and higher weight decay (~0.005) - these drove stability\n- Continue monitoring accuracy variance (std_accuracy) as your most sensitive performance indicator\n- Preserve batch normalization and current dropout approach (they're working adequately)\n\n**What to Change:**\n- **Stop scaling complexity indiscriminately** - the weak correlation (0.266) for parameters signals diminishing returns\n- **Test architectural efficiency** - compare your best performers against standardized architectures (ResNet, EfficientNet) with similar compute budgets\n- **Introduce dynamic early stopping** instead of fixed 50 epochs - let performance determine training length\n\n**New Hypothesis:**\n*Optimal performance comes from architectural sufficiency (not maximization) combined with rigorous training stabilization. The highest accuracy gains will come from improving learning dynamics rather than adding parameters.*\n\n**Actionable Experiments:**\n1. **Efficiency Benchmark:** Take your current best architecture and create scaled-down versions (50%, 25% parameters) with identical training protocols\n2. **Stability Optimization:** Fix architecture at median complexity and systematically optimize learning rate \u00d7 weight decay combinations\n3. **Component Ablation:** Remove individual components (extra layers, large kernels) from best performers to identify true drivers\n\n**Strategic Priority:** Shift from \"what makes accuracy higher\" to \"what makes improvement efficient.\" Your next breakthrough will come from smarter optimization, not larger models.", "experiment_name": "2D_SPECTROGRAM"}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.05450000000000001, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
</edge>
