<edge source="2D_GAF_eb7050af" target="2D_GAF_eb7050af" id="memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 75 (for th...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 75 (for th...)</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Consolidated summary at step 75 (for the last block of research):\n**STRATEGIC LESSON: Optimization Phase 2**\n\n**CORE INSIGHT:** We're optimizing for memorization, not generalization. The current approach favors brute-force capacity over intelligent architecture.\n\n**WHAT TO KEEP:**\n- **Architecture trends:** Continue exploring larger kernel sizes (7-9) and moderate filter increases\n- **Training strategy:** Maintain low learning rates (~0.0001) and moderate dropout (0.5-0.6)\n- **Performance targets:** Continue prioritizing low validation loss and stable accuracy\n\n**WHAT TO CHANGE:**\n- **Priority shift:** Optimize for parameter efficiency, not just absolute accuracy\n- **Regularization:** Strengthen weight decay and batch normalization to combat overfitting\n- **Evaluation:** Add cross-validation and focus on generalization gap (test vs train accuracy)\n\n**CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS:**\n- Cap parameter growth: Target &lt;15M parameters maximum\n- Monitor generalization gap: Keep test accuracy within 5% of training accuracy\n- Balance inference speed: Maintain &lt;20ms while improving accuracy\n\n**NEW HYPOTHESIS:** \n\"Architectures with efficient feature extraction (moderate filters + strategic kernel sizing) and strong regularization will achieve &gt;95% accuracy with &lt;60% of current parameter counts, demonstrating better generalization through reduced train-test performance gaps.\"\n\n**IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n1. Run constrained NAS with parameter caps and enhanced regularization\n2. Add generalization metrics as primary optimization targets\n3. Test architectural efficiency via performance-per-parameter ratios\n\n**STRATEGIC PRIORITY:** Quality over quantity - smarter architectures, not just larger ones.", "experiment_name": "2D_GAF"}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.0407381, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
</edge>
