<edge source="2D_GAF_b815df2c" target="2D_GAF_b815df2c" id="memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 50 (for th...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 50 (for th...)</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Consolidated summary at step 50 (for the last block of research):\n### Strategic Lesson: The Efficiency-Robustness Trade-off\n\n**Core Insight:** Performance is primarily driven by model capacity and training stability, but our current \"best\" models are likely over-parameterized and brittle. The optimal strategy shifts from pure accuracy maximization to balancing performance with efficiency and generalization.\n\n---\n\n### Actionable Directives for Next Phase:\n\n**1. KEEP the Foundation**\n- **Continue leveraging** the strong correlation between lower validation loss/higher learning speed and final performance\n- **Maintain focus** on smaller batch sizes (16-32) and lower learning rates (~0.0007) as starting points\n- **Preserve** the architectural trend toward moderate depth (10-12 convolutional layers)\n\n**2. CHANGE the Optimization Priority**\n- **Shift from accuracy-centric to efficiency-aware optimization**\n- **Introduce computational constraints** (parameter count &lt; 8M, inference latency targets)\n- **Implement stronger regularization** specifically for high-capacity models (L2, dropout with expanded search ranges)\n\n**3. INVESTIGATE Critical Interactions**\n- **Test hypothesis:** \"Optimal learning rate scales inversely with model size\"\n- **Explore** whether smaller models with more aggressive regularization can match larger models' accuracy\n- **Validate** if the current train-test gap (7.3%) can be reduced to &lt;5% without sacrificing performance\n\n---\n\n### New Strategic Hypothesis:\n\"The Pareto-optimal solution lies in moderately-sized architectures (8-10M parameters) with dynamically-scaled regularization, where learning rate and batch size are tuned as functions of model capacity rather than treated as independent variables.\"\n\n**Key Metric Shift:** Track accuracy-per-parameter and robustness scores (performance on corrupted data) alongside raw accuracy. The best model is no longer the most accurate one, but the most accurate one within computational constraints that generalizes reliably.", "experiment_name": "2D_GAF"}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.032912707159982124, 0.009808828313692838, 0.004278431877470253, 1.1878092569077559, 6.283710046834006]</data>
</edge>
